        "original_id": "d9dfb7c2-2890-53be-8ffc-876dd88219ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Yuh-Line Niou, Sheldon Silver, Alice Cancel, Joseph D. Morelle\n- Organizations: Democratic Party, New York State Assembly\n- Roles: Assembly member, Speaker, Majority Leader\n- Places: New York City, New York\n\nFacts:\n- Sheldon Silver was born on February 13, 1944.\n- In 1994, Sheldon Silver became Speaker of the New York State Assembly.\n- In January 2013, Speaker Sheldon Silver appointed Joseph D. Morelle as Majority Leader of the New York State Assembly.\n- In 2015, Sheldon Silver's time as Speaker ended when he was arrested on federal corruption charges.\n- In 2016, Alice Cancel was defeated in the Democratic primary for her seat by Yuh-Line Niou.\n- Yuh-Line Niou is a Democratic Party member of the New York State Assembly for the 65th district.\n- Yuh-Line Niou holds the New York State Assembly seat for the 65th district that was previously held by Sheldon Silver.\n- Sheldon Silver is a former lawyer and Democratic Party politician from New York City.",
